E["npc:arcanist-doan"] = {t="npc",n="Arcanist Doan",z="scarlet",s="Within the Scarlet Monastery, Arcanist Doan guards the Athenaeum and its archives. A master human mage, he brings deadly arcane skill to the Scarlet Crusade.",h="Within the Scarlet Monastery, Arcanist Doan guards the Athenaeum and its archives.",sec={{t="Keeper of the Athenaeum",b="The Scarlet Crusade trusts martial fury and holy fervor. Doan believes arcane power is vital to driving the Scourge from Lordaeron. Deep in the Monastery's library, he keeps its lore and guards the Scarlet Key. That key secures Crusade sanctuaries across the northern kingdoms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a mage in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is ruled by zealous paladins and priests. Doan believes masterful arcane magic is essential to cleansing Lordaeron of the Scourge.",al={"why is doan a mage","crusade mage","doan magic"},it="side"},{q="What is Arcanist Doan's connection to the Ashbringer?",a="Doan has no known connection to the Ashbringer. He guards the Scarlet Monastery's library and the Scarlet Key.",al={"doan ashbringer","did doan make ashbringer","ashbringer crystal"},it="ties"},{q="What does Doan guard in the Library?",a="Doan guards the Athenaeum's books and historical records. A lockbox behind him holds the Scarlet Key, which opens the locked gates to the Monastery's Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"what does doan drop","scarlet key","why kill doan"},it="why_here"},{q="What magic does Doan use in combat?",a="Doan can cast an Arcane Bubble that makes him invulnerable while he channels a massive Detonation spell that fills the room. He can also silence spellcasters across an area and turn threats into sheep.",al={"doan spells","doan abilities","arcanist doan bubble"},it="power"},{q="Where did Doan fight during the Third War?",a="No deeds of Doan during the Third War are recorded. Today he guards the Scarlet Monastery's Athenaeum and the Scarlet Key.",al={"doan war history","where was doan"},it="history"},{q="Does Doan harbor any personal secrets?",a="Doan serves the Scarlet Crusade as an arcanist. No record speaks of his private romantic attachments.",al={"doan lore"}},{q="Who is Arcanist Doan?",a="Arcanist Doan is a human mage and one of the most powerful arcane practitioners serving the Scarlet Crusade. He resides deep within the Athenaeum of the Scarlet Monastery's Library, where he keeps the order's archives and the Scarlet Key, wielding devastating arcane magic in defense of the order's holy sanctuary.",al={"who is doan","arcanist doan lore","doan scarlet monastery"},it="identity",add="979d2c44"},{q="What does Arcanist Doan want?",a="Doan is driven by the conviction that arcane magic is the only true way to completely cleanse Lordaeron of the Scourge. While his Scarlet Crusade brethren rely almost entirely upon the zealotry of the Holy Light, Doan believes raw arcane power and study are necessary to contain and eradicate the undead plague once and for all.",al={"doan goals","what does doan want","arcanist doan motive"},it="wants",add="46f867c9"},{q="Why is Arcanist Doan feared?",a="Doan is feared as one of the most formidable mages in Lordaeron. In battle he encases himself in a nearly impenetrable Arcane Bubble to channel cataclysmic Detonation spells, capable of incinerating entire groups of intruders in an instant.",al={"why is doan feared","how strong is doan","doan reputation"},it="fame",add="88b26aa6"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can see Doan's mastery of arcane defenses in the protective bubble he casts.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you meet a rare arcanist trusted by the Scarlet Crusade, an order that prizes the Light above all other powers.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance fighter, you see how the Scarlet Crusade's zeal binds even a master of the arcane to its violent paranoia.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a dangerous Scarlet commander whose library holds vital intelligence and keys to the Crusade's inner sanctums."},kw={"arcanist","athenaeum","detonation","doan","library","scarlet key","scarlet monastery"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge"},src={"Arcanist Doan"}}
E["npc:bloodmage-thalnos"] = {t="npc",n="Bloodmage Thalnos",z="scarlet",s="In the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard, Bloodmage Thalnos haunts the tombs, hungry for vengeance. The plague of undeath claimed him, and he remains deep within the Crusade's holy grounds.",h="In the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard, Bloodmage Thalnos haunts the tombs, hungry for vengeance.",sec={{t="A Mage Risen in Death",b="No record tells who Thalnos was in life. The plague of undeath claimed him, and he rose as a withered skeleton. Still, he clings to fiery magic and arcane mastery. He cries out for vengeance and more souls.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Graveyard",b="From the deepest corner of the monastery's courtyard tombs, Thalnos commands apparitions and shambling undead minions. He attacks anyone who disturbs his domain. Beneath the Crusade's sacred halls, his presence is a bitter contradiction. He embodies the horror they swore to eradicate.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bloodmage Thalnos?",a="Bloodmage Thalnos haunts the Scarlet Monastery's graveyard as a skeletal spellcaster. No record tells who he was in life; the plague of undeath claimed him, and he rose as an undead mage hungry for vengeance.",al={"who is thalnos","thalnos lore","bloodmage thalnos info"},it="identity"},{q="Why is an undead skeleton allowed in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Crusade executes undead on sight, yet Thalnos remains at the far end of the Graveyard among risen crypts and spirits. He prowls his own blighted domain rather than walking freely among the living crusaders.",al={"why is thalnos in monastery","why does scarlet crusade keep thalnos","scarlet crusade undead mage"},it="why_here"},{q="What powers does Thalnos wield?",a="Thalnos commands fiery spells and shadow magic. He also summons vengeful spirits and walking dead to overwhelm trespassers in the graveyard.",al={"thalnos spells","bloodmage thalnos magic","what does thalnos do"},it="power"},{q="Was Thalnos a blood elf?",a="Thalnos's mortal lineage is uncertain. The title Bloodmage alone does not establish that he was a blood elf.",al={"is thalnos high elf","thalnos race","what race was thalnos"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants Thalnos dead?",a="Thalnos is hostile to intruders in the monastery's graveyard. No specific commission to kill him is established for this era.",al={"thalnos quest","who wants thalnos killed","the dark side of the light thalnos"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Bloodmage Thalnos on?",a="Thalnos serves no one. After succumbing to the plague of undeath, he became a creature entirely driven by vengeance and unholy power. Now an undead skeleton, he fiercely guards his own domain within the monastery's graveyard, commanding apparitions and zombified creatures to slaughter any living trespassers who cross his path.",al={"thalnos faction","who does thalnos serve","is thalnos scarlet crusade"},it="side",add="ee50c387"},{q="What does Bloodmage Thalnos want?",a="Driven mad by undeath, Thalnos desires little more than unholy vengeance. Bound to the monastery's graveyard, the vengeful skeletal mage commands restless apparitions and reanimated corpses to eradicate anyone who dares enter his cursed territory.",al={"what does thalnos want","thalnos goal","thalnos motives"},it="wants",add="fb23ba27"},{q="Why is Bloodmage Thalnos feared?",a="Thalnos is a powerful undead spellcaster who rules the monastery's graveyard, hurling fire and shadow at intruders and crying out for vengeance and more souls. That such a creature lurks among the Scarlet Crusade's own dead makes him all the more unsettling.",al={"why is thalnos feared","what made thalnos famous","bloodmage thalnos reputation"},it="fame",add="39b55bcf"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, Thalnos shows how the plague can twist a gifted spellcaster into a vengeful being who still wields fire and shadow.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may see in Thalnos what the Forsaken escaped: an undead mage with no will left but vengeance, lurking in the heart of the Scarlet Crusade's monastery.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see in Thalnos among the tombs an unsettling sign that the Crusade's zeal has not kept darkness from its holy ground."},kw={"bloodmage","graveyard","scarlet monastery","skeleton","thalnos"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:light"},src={"Bloodmage Thalnos"}}
E["npc:herod"] = {t="npc",n="Herod",z="scarlet",s="In the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, Herod trains the Crusade's melee fighters. A renowned champion, he commands the Armory and wages the Crusade's holy war with fierce skill and zeal. Alliance dissidents and the Horde's rulers in Undercity seek his death to weaken the order.",h="In the Scarlet Monastery's Armory, Herod trains the Crusade's melee fighters.",sec={{t="The Champion of the Armory",b="Herod commands the Armory within the Scarlet Monastery. Unlike the spellcasters and paladins in the Cathedral, he relies on physical strength. Clad in mail and bearing a massive two-handed axe, he trains cohorts of Scarlet Trainees. He teaches them to fight with fury and destroy anyone beyond the Crusade's cause.",sp=0},{t="A High-Priority Target",b="Herod oversees the weapons and combat training of the Crusade's front-line warriors. Raleigh the Devout, an ex-Crusader disillusioned with the order's madness, lives in Southshore and calls for Herod's death to break its military leadership. In the Undercity, the dreadlord Varimathras also seeks Herod's execution. He wants the dangerous human stronghold cleared from the border of Forsaken territory.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Herod?",a="Herod is a human warrior who commands the Armory in the Scarlet Monastery. He is one of the Monastery's four principal leaders and oversees the equipment and training of the Crusade's devoted melee fighters.",al={"herod lore","who is herod","herod scarlet monastery"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Herod located?",a="Herod waits in a central training ring in the Scarlet Monastery's Armory wing, in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Viewing galleries surround the ring.",al={"where is herod","herod location","find herod"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Horde want Herod dead?",a="Varimathras seeks Herod's death on behalf of the Forsaken in the Undercity. He wants to remove a key Scarlet Monastery commander and end the Crusade's threat near Forsaken territory.",al={"varimathras herod quest","why horde kill herod","into the scarlet monastery"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Alliance want Herod dead?",a="Raleigh the Devout asks Alliance champions to kill Herod. The former Scarlet Crusader, stationed in Hillsbrad Foothills, sees the order's fanatical zealotry and wants its brutal warrior leadership weakened.",al={"in the name of the light","raleigh the devout herod","why alliance kill herod"},it="motive"},{q="What happens when Herod is defeated?",a="When Herod falls, young Scarlet Trainees rush from the surrounding barracks into the ring to avenge him. Their attack shows the devotion he inspired in his students.",al={"scarlet trainees","herod trainee rush","herod death event"},sp=1,gp=true},{q="What kind of fighter is Herod?",a="Herod is a berserker and a warrior, not a traditional holy paladin. He charges viciously and unleashes sweeping whirlwind strikes, relying on physical fury instead of Holy Light spells.",al={"herod fighting style","is herod a paladin"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Herod on?",a="Herod is a high-ranking commander of the Scarlet Crusade, serving as one of the four key leaders stationed within the Scarlet Monastery. Fanatically loyal to the Crusade's zealous mission, he directs their military training and armory against any and all whom the Crusade deems impure or hostile.",al={"herod faction","who does herod serve","what side is herod on"},it="side",add="3c3e6bcb"},{q="What does Herod want?",a="Herod is dedicated to preparing the Scarlet Crusade's next generation of warriors to eradicate their enemies. Overseeing the Armory, he drills trainees to match his own relentless martial fervor, seeking to crush anyone foolish enough to trespass upon the Monastery's sacred grounds.",al={"herod goal","herod purpose","what is herod trying to do"},it="wants",add="78320a40"},{q="Why is Herod here?",a="Herod commands the Armory wing of the Scarlet Monastery. As the champion and trainer of the Scarlet trainees, he oversees the Crusade's arsenal and personally tests anyone who dares challenge the Crusade's heartland.",al={"why is herod in the armory","why is herod at scarlet monastery","herod armory role"},it="why_here",add="60fea3ae"},{q="Who is Herod tied to?",a="Herod stands alongside the inner leadership of the Scarlet Monastery, which includes High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine, and Houndmaster Loksey. Together, they govern the Crusade's bastion in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"who leads herod","herod allies","who does herod work with"},it="ties",add="f73350c1"},{q="Why is Herod famous or feared?",a="Known as the Scarlet Champion, Herod is renowned for his ferocious, berserker fighting style. Wielding a massive battleaxe, he is infamous for spinning into a devastating, unstoppable whirlwind of steel that rends all nearby foes to pieces.",al={"why is herod feared","herod reputation","what makes herod dangerous"},it="fame",add="9c060a47"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, Herod shows how furious whirlwind strikes and reckless aggression can make a fighter feared among the Scarlet Crusade's recruits.",["faction:Horde"]="For the Horde, especially the Forsaken, killing Herod carries out Varimathras's order to break the leadership threatening Tirisfal Glades.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero answering Raleigh the Devout's plea, you can see how leaders like Herod have driven Lordaeron's once-noble defenders into fanatical bloodlust."},kw={"armory","berserker","herod","raleigh the devout","ravager","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","varimathras"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","npc:varimathras","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","topic:light"},src={"Herod"}}
E["npc:high-inquisitor-fairbanks"] = {t="npc",n="High Inquisitor Fairbanks",z="scarlet",s="In the Scarlet Crusade, High Inquisitor Fairbanks's fate remains bound to the order's dark descent. Before Lordaeron fell, he was a revered priest and a trusted advisor to Highlord Alexandros Mograine.",h="In the Scarlet Crusade, High Inquisitor Fairbanks's fate remains bound to the order's dark descent.",sec={{t="Advisor to the Ashbringer",b="Before Lordaeron fell, Fairbanks was a respected priest of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Highlord Alexandros Mograine trusted him above all others. Mograine bore the Ashbringer. Fairbanks stood beside Mograine, High General Abbendis and Grand Inquisitor Isillien when they founded the Scarlet Crusade, an order sworn to destroy the Scourge.",sp=0},{t="Betrayal at Stratholme",b="Fairbanks accompanied Alexandros Mograine when Renault, the Highlord’s eldest son, led them into a Scourge ambush outside Stratholme. Undead claws brought Fairbanks down early, and heaps of rotting corpses buried him. Beneath them, he saw Renault take the fallen Ashbringer and drive it into his father’s heart. The patricide corrupted the holy blade.\n\nFairbanks survived the slaughter and clawed free of the dead. He returned to the Scarlet Monastery to expose Renault’s treachery.",sp=1},{t="Execution and Exile",b="Fairbanks’s warnings split Lordaeron’s remaining defenders. Those who believed him left the fanatical order and formed the Argent Dawn. Those still loyal to Renault and Saidan Dathrohan branded him a blasphemer and lunatic.\n\nThe Scarlet Crusade executed Fairbanks in secret. The crusaders denied him a holy burial and cast his body into a hidden chamber behind the Cathedral’s altar. There, he eventually rose as the very monstrosity they had sworn to cleanse.",sp=2}},faq={{q="Where can I find High Inquisitor Fairbanks?",a="Fairbanks lies hidden in the Cathedral wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Enter the side chapel to the right of the main altar and pull the concealed wall torch. It opens a secret stone doorway into a secluded crypt.",al={"where is fairbanks","how to find fairbanks","fairbanks secret room","monastery secret door"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Fairbanks an undead creature?",a="No one has explained exactly how Fairbanks rose. At Stratholme, he lay buried beneath piles of Scourge corpses. After the Scarlet Crusade executed him for accusing its leaders, they cast his body into a hidden chamber, where it eventually rose as undead.",al={"why is fairbanks a zombie","is fairbanks scourge","why is fairbanks undead"},sp=2,it="origin"},{q="Who was Fairbanks before he was executed?",a="Before his execution, Fairbanks was a devout priest of the Knights of the Silver Hand and chief counselor to Highlord Alexandros Mograine, bearer of the Ashbringer. He was among the original spiritual leaders of Lordaeron’s surviving defenders.",al={"fairbanks backstory","who is high inquisitor fairbanks","fairbanks lore"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the split between the Scarlet Crusade and the Argent Dawn?",a="Fairbanks’s account of what he witnessed at Stratholme fractured the order. Those who believed him and rejected Renault’s fanaticism left to establish the Argent Dawn. Renault’s zealots remained with the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"argent dawn origin","why did argent dawn split","fairbanks argent dawn"},sp=2,it="conflict"},{q="Why did the Scarlet Crusade kill Fairbanks?",a="The Scarlet Crusade’s leaders called Fairbanks’s testimony about Stratholme malicious blasphemy. They executed him to silence the truth.",al={"why did scarlet kill fairbanks","who killed fairbanks","fairbanks execution"},sp=2,it="history"},{q="Who replaced Fairbanks as High Inquisitor?",a="After Fairbanks’s execution and secret imprisonment, Whitemane became High Inquisitor. She led the Scarlet Monastery’s inquisitorial interrogations alongside Commander Renault Mograine.",al={"who is high inquisitor now","fairbanks replacement","who succeeded fairbanks"},it="leader"},{q="Whose side is High Inquisitor Fairbanks on now?",a="Fairbanks belongs to no faction anymore. While he was once a revered priest of the Silver Hand and Highlord Alexandros Mograine's closest confidant, his murder and subsequent rise into undeath stripped him of his mind and former allegiances. Consumed by the plague of undeath and locked away by the very zealots he once guided, he is utterly hostile to any living being that enters his hidden tomb, lashing out in mindless agony and madness.",al={"fairbanks faction","is fairbanks hostile","fairbanks side"},sp=1,it="side",add="14cc9219"},{q="Why is Fairbanks hidden in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="After surviving the ambush at Stratholme, Fairbanks returned to the Scarlet Monastery and spoke out against the Crusade's leaders, Renault Mograine and Saidan Dathrohan. Branded a heretic and liar, he was executed to silence him. The Crusaders then discarded his body in a hidden chamber behind the Cathedral altar, leaving his reanimated corpse sealed away in secret.",al={"why is fairbanks in the monastery","fairbanks hidden room why","fairbanks secret chamber"},sp=2,it="why_here",add="d7d74c1e"},{q="Who was High Inquisitor Fairbanks tied to?",a="Fairbanks was the closest advisor and companion to Highlord Alexandros Mograine, the legendary Ashbringer, and stood beside him when Mograine, High General Abbendis and Grand Inquisitor Isillien founded the Scarlet Crusade. He rode with Alexandros to Stratholme, and what he witnessed there drove him to warn the other knights, a warning that inspired the schism that founded the Argent Dawn.",al={"fairbanks connections","fairbanks mograine","who did fairbanks serve"},sp=1,it="ties",add="edd0ed20"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Fairbanks witnessed the Silver Hand’s darkest hour, when an honored paladin turned a legendary holy blade against his own father.",["class:Priest"]="Before his fall, Fairbanks was a priest of the Light and Highlord Mograine’s closest counselor.",["race:Undead"]="Fairbanks reveals the Scarlet Crusade’s hypocrisy: they hid one of their own dead behind an altar while burning innocent Forsaken.",["faction:Alliance"]="Fairbanks’s tragedy began in fallen Lordaeron, where the Grand Alliance’s remnants split into zealots and outcasts."},kw={"ashbringer","cathedral","fairbanks","inquisitor","mograine","renault","scarlet monastery","silver hand","stratholme"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:knights-of-the-silver-hand","topic:argent-dawn","subzone:stratholme","npc:tirion-fordring"},src={"High Inquisitor Fairbanks"}}
E["npc:houndmaster-loksey"] = {t="npc",n="Houndmaster Loksey",z="scarlet",s="In the Scarlet Monastery's Library wing, Houndmaster Loksey keeps the Crusade's war dogs ready. He breeds and trains them to hunt undead, intruders, and those the Crusade judges heretics. His harsh discipline has made the Monastery's beasts feared across Tirisfal Glades.",h="In the Scarlet Monastery's Library wing, Houndmaster Loksey keeps the Crusade's war dogs ready.",sec={{t="Master of the Kennels",b="Houndmaster Loksey trains vicious dogs to track and attack. The Scarlet Crusade sends them to sniff out plague-tainted corpses, uncover hidden infiltrators, and run down survivors fleeing the zealots' wrath. Loksey commands the hounds guarding the Library wing. They stand ready to tear intruders limb from limb.",sp=0},{t="Family Rivalry",b="Loksey's brother, Huntsman Leopold, serves the Scarlet Crusade as its envoy to the Argent Dawn at Light's Hope Chapel. In private, Leopold thinks Loksey can barely manage his hounds, let alone handle high-stakes diplomacy. Yet Loksey remains a key officer in the Monastery's inner hierarchy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Houndmaster Loksey be found?",a="Houndmaster Loksey can be found in the Library wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, surrounded by his attack dogs.",al={"loksey location","where is loksey","houndmaster loksey location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Loksey serve in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Loksey is the Scarlet Crusade's chief animal handler and houndmaster at the Monastery. He breeds, trains, and directs war dogs that sniff out undead and hunt intruders.",al={"what does loksey do","loksey job","houndmaster duty"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Huntsman Leopold to Loksey?",a="Huntsman Leopold is Loksey's brother. He represents the Scarlet Crusade at Light's Hope Chapel and looks down on Loksey, believing he cannot manage his hounds or handle diplomacy.",al={"leopold loksey brother","who is leopold","loksey brother"},it="ties"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade use hounds?",a="The Scarlet Crusade trains vicious hounds to track the Scourge and Forsaken by scent, guard the Monastery's grounds, and tear fleeing enemies to pieces.",al={"why dogs","scarlet hounds purpose","crusade dogs"}},{q="Is Loksey considered a leader of the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Yes. Loksey is a key commanding figure in the Scarlet Monastery's military structure. He oversees the Crusade's war hounds in the Library wing.",al={"is loksey a boss","loksey rank","how important is loksey"},it="leader"},{q="Are the hounds dangerous on their own?",a="Yes. Bred for aggression and trained by Loksey, the Monastery's war hounds can rip an armored intruder limb from limb in moments.",al={"are dogs strong","scarlet hounds danger","loksey pets"},it="danger"},{q="Who is Houndmaster Loksey?",a="Houndmaster Loksey is a human captain and one of the four commanders residing within the Scarlet Monastery. Renowned for his brutal discipline, he serves as the kennel master responsible for breeding, conditioning, and unleashing the Crusade's vicious hounds upon intruders and suspected carriers of the undead taint.",al={"who is loksey","houndmaster loksey identity","who is houndmaster loksey"},it="identity",add="92e01b8b"},{q="Whose side is Houndmaster Loksey on?",a="Loksey is staunchly devoted to the Scarlet Crusade, serving as a frontline commander within their monastery stronghold. He shares the Crusade's fanatical hatred for the undead and anyone outside their zealot order, viewing any who encroach upon their halls as interlopers fit only to feed his kennel.",al={"loksey faction","houndmaster loksey alliance","who does loksey serve"},it="side",add="6cbd929d"},{q="What does Houndmaster Loksey want?",a="Loksey aims to defend the Scarlet Monastery by training ruthless hunting packs capable of tearing any enemy apart limb by limb. He wants to scour every trace of the undead and protect Crusade territory from outsiders, using his beasts to hunt down intruders without hesitation or mercy.",al={"loksey goal","what is loksey trying to do","houndmaster loksey motive"},it="wants",add="1361b0af"},{q="Why is Houndmaster Loksey here?",a="Loksey is stationed in the Monastery's library wing to oversee the Crusader kennels. As houndmaster, he must ensure the hounds remain sharp, aggressively conditioned, and ready to be loosed at a moment's notice to patrol the grounds and slaughter intruders.",al={"why is loksey at the monastery","why is houndmaster loksey here","loksey purpose"},it="why_here",add="58572016"},{q="Why is Houndmaster Loksey famous or feared?",a="Loksey is feared for his pack of trained hounds, beasts known to overpower and tear victims to shreds within minutes. Anyone venturing into the monastery dreads encountering his kennel, knowing Loksey's vicious command turns his animals into unrelenting engines of carnage.",al={"why is loksey feared","loksey reputation","why is houndmaster loksey dangerous"},it="fame",add="264719ea"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="Loksey trains beasts with brutal force. His fierce hounds obey zealotry, not mutual respect.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, beware Loksey's hounds. They are trained to catch the scent of dead flesh and alert the Crusade's garrisons."},kw={"library","houndmaster loksey","hounds","huntsman leopold","kennels","loksey","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:light-s-hope-chapel","topic:argent-dawn","topic:alliance"},src={"Houndmaster Loksey"}}
E["npc:interrogator-vishas"] = {t="npc",n="Interrogator Vishas",z="scarlet",s="Deep in the Scarlet Monastery, Interrogator Vishas has captives at his mercy. The Scarlet Crusade’s master of torment takes pleasure in breaking prisoners and testing mortal flesh.",h="Deep in the Scarlet Monastery, Interrogator Vishas has captives at his mercy.",sec={{t="The Grand Inquisitor's Scalpel",b="In the Scarlet Monastery’s crypts and burial grounds, Interrogator Vishas tends the Crusade’s captives. Outside, zealots march in gleaming armor beneath banners of purity. Inside, Vishas reveals the cruelty behind their righteous fury.\n\nInterrogation serves the Crusade’s need for intelligence, and Vishas prizes it as a craft. He revels in the agony of Forsaken captives, captured Scourge, and living travelers branded heretics.",sp=0},{t="A Life of Quiet Domesticity",b="Far from the torture chamber, Interrogator Vishas keeps a strange domestic life. His wife, Nancy Vishas, and his elder relative, Grandpa Vishas, live peacefully in an isolated cottage on Lordamere Lake’s eastern shore in the Alterac Mountains.\n\nVishas took a cherished wedding ring from Vorrel Sengutz, his Forsaken captive, and carried it home as a gift for Nancy.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Interrogator Vishas be found?",a="Interrogator Vishas can be found deep in the Scarlet Monastery’s Graveyard wing in Tirisfal Glades. His torture chamber is lined with iron cages and bloodied racks.",al={"vishas location","where is interrogator vishas","vishas room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Vishas torture his prisoners?",a="The Scarlet Crusade tortures captives to root out Scourge corruption and extract information. Vishas delights in causing pain, takes pride in his cruelty, and regards torture as his craft.",al={"why is vishas torturing people","vishas motivation"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Vorrel Sengutz?",a="Vorrel Sengutz is a Forsaken captive whom Interrogator Vishas imprisoned and tortured in the Monastery’s Graveyard. After weeks of pain, Vorrel lost his wedding band to Vishas, who meant it as a gift for his wife.",al={"vorrel sengutz prisoner","who is the prisoner in the cage"},it="target"},{q="Where does Vishas' family live?",a="Vishas’s family lives far from the Monastery in an unassuming cottage on the eastern bank of Lordamere Lake in the Alterac Mountains. Nancy and Grandpa Vishas live there quietly, seemingly detached from his atrocities.",al={"nancy vishas location","grandpa vishas","vishas family house"},it="ties"},{q="Who does Vishas hold prisoner?",a="The Scarlet Crusade regards the undead as enemies. Interrogator Vishas holds the Forsaken Vorrel Sengutz prisoner and has tortured him for weeks.",al={"vishas prisoners","who does vishas torture","vishas captive vorrel"}},{q="What is Vishas' voice and demeanor like?",a="Among those who face him, Interrogator Vishas is infamous for his grating, high-pitched voice and cackling laughter. He shows disturbing excitement when trying to tear secrets from an unwilling victim.",al={"vishas voice","vishas personality"},it="fame"},{q="Who is Interrogator Vishas?",a="James Vishas is the chief interrogator of the Scarlet Crusade, stationed within the depths of the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard. Fanatical and notoriously cruel, he takes immense pride in breaking prisoners brought before him. Armed with torture implements and an unhinged zeal, he extracts confessions and torment in equal measure from anyone unfortunate enough to fall into his hands.",al={"who is vishas","interrogator vishas lore","who is james vishas"},it="identity",add="518fe48c"},{q="Whose side is Interrogator Vishas on?",a="Vishas is entirely devoted to the Scarlet Crusade. He serves their zealous crusade by torturing suspected Scourge agents, Forsaken prisoners, and anyone else deemed tainted or hostile to the order's fanatical purity.",al={"vishas faction","who does vishas work for","vishas scarlet crusade"},it="side",add="cadee917"},{q="Why is Interrogator Vishas here?",a="Vishas is stationed in the torture chambers of the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard to handle prisoners captured across Tirisfal Glades. He spends his days and nights extracting information, venting sadistic urges, and breaking the spirits of captives like Vorrel Sengutz on behalf of the Crusade.",al={"why is vishas in the graveyard","vishas monastery role","what is vishas doing here"},it="why_here",add="e1510cf6"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, Interrogator Vishas embodies the living zealots’ hypocrisy. He tortures captured undead out of spite while claiming to serve the Holy Light.",["faction:Alliance"]="When you discover Interrogator Vishas’s work, you see that the Scarlet Crusade no longer distinguishes Scourge monsters from innocent living travelers.",["class:Priest"]="When you see Interrogator Vishas use zealotry to sanctify horrific mutilation, you witness how holy purpose can curdle into twisted madness."},kw={"graveyard","interrogator vishas","james vishas","lordamere lake","nancy vishas","scarlet monastery","torture","vorrel sengutz"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:lordamere-lake","zone:alterac","topic:light"},src={"Interrogator Vishas"}}
E["npc:sally-whitemane"] = {t="npc",n="High Inquisitor Whitemane",z="scarlet",s="At the Scarlet Monastery, High Inquisitor Whitemane directs the Crusade from its Cathedral. A priestess of the Holy Light, she drives the order’s zeal with a consuming hatred of the undead. Alongside Scarlet Commander Renault Mograine, she leads its military and ideological campaigns across Lordaeron.",h="At the Scarlet Monastery, High Inquisitor Whitemane directs the Crusade from its Cathedral.",sec={{t="High Inquisitor of the Crusade",b="Whitemane rose swiftly through the Scarlet Crusade. Now she commands the grand Cathedral of the Scarlet Monastery as its High Inquisitor. Her mastery of Holy magic is feared, and her unshakable conviction makes her one of the Crusade’s foremost symbols. She brings the Light against all she deems unclean without mercy.",sp=0},{t="Targets in the Cathedral",b="After the Third War, Whitemane’s fanaticism has made enemies on both sides. In Southshore, Raleigh the Devout believes the Crusade has fallen into corruption and madness. He calls for Whitemane and Mograine to be eliminated so the order may return to its founding virtues.\n\nIn the Undercity, dreadlord Varimathras directs attacks on the Monastery. He means to crush the zealots working on the Forsaken’s doorstep.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is High Inquisitor Whitemane?",a="Whitemane leads the Scarlet Crusade as its High Inquisitor. From the Cathedral inside the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, she commands the order’s spiritual and inquisitorial efforts alongside Commander Renault Mograine.",al={"whitemane lore","who is high inquisitor whitemane","scarlet monastery boss"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Whitemane hate the undead so much?",a="Whitemane’s hatred follows the Scarlet Crusade’s creed. The order rose from survivors of Lordaeron’s fall to the plague of undeath, and calls every undead an abomination to be purged, whether mindless or free-willed. Whitemane wields the Holy Light relentlessly in that war.",al={"why does whitemane hate scourge","whitemane backstory","whitemane family"},it="motive"},{q="Why does the Alliance want Whitemane dead?",a="Raleigh the Devout, a former Crusader in Southshore, believes the Scarlet Crusade has sunk into paranoia and madness. He asks Alliance champions to eliminate Whitemane and Mograine, hoping the order can return to its honorable origins.",al={"raleigh the devout whitemane","why kill whitemane alliance","in the name of the light quest"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does the Horde want Whitemane dead?",a="Varimathras and the Forsaken in the Undercity see the Scarlet Crusade as a hostile force at their capital’s doorstep. The dreadlord orders Whitemane’s death to break the Monastery’s leadership and remove an immediate threat to the Forsaken realm.",al={"varimathras whitemane quest","into the scarlet monastery","why horde kills whitemane"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Whitemane's relationship with Renault Mograine?",a="Whitemane and Renault Mograine lead the Scarlet Monastery together. They fight side by side in the Cathedral, bound by an intimate bond and mutual devotion to the Crusade’s war against undeath.",al={"whitemane and mograine","commander mograine and whitemane"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is High Inquisitor Whitemane on?",a="Whitemane is a zealous leader of the Scarlet Crusade, serving as their High Inquisitor. She owes no allegiance to the Alliance or the Horde, viewing outsiders with extreme suspicion and fanaticism. Whitemane is fiercely loyal to the Crusade's dogma, fighting alongside Commander Renault Mograine to purge any who stand in their path.",al={"whitemane faction","who does whitemane fight for","whitemane allegiance"},it="side",add="f63bdc05"},{q="What does High Inquisitor Whitemane want?",a="Whitemane desires the utter eradication of the undead. Like the rest of the Scarlet Crusade, she sees every undead creature, mindless Scourge or free-willed Forsaken, as an abomination. She finds purpose only in purging the Scourge and anyone she deems tainted by undeath.",al={"whitemane goals","what does whitemane want","whitemane motivation"},it="wants",add="89d62c4b"},{q="Why is High Inquisitor Whitemane here?",a="As High Inquisitor, Whitemane directs the Scarlet Crusade's operations from deep within the Scarlet Monastery's Cathedral. There she oversees the defense of their northern Lordaeron sanctuary, rallying the crusaders and purging all who trespass upon their holy stronghold.",al={"why is whitemane in the monastery","whitemane cathedral why","why is whitemane here"},it="why_here",add="04c4cc89"},{q="Why is High Inquisitor Whitemane famous or feared?",a="Whitemane is feared for her unyielding fanatical zeal and her formidable mastery of holy magic. As the High Inquisitor of the Scarlet Crusade, she has earned a terrifying reputation for ruthlessly purging suspected corruption and raising fallen allies, including Commander Mograine, in the midst of battle.",al={"why is whitemane feared","whitemane reputation","why is whitemane famous"},it="fame",add="7daae460"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="For a priest, Whitemane shows the terrible power of the Holy Light joined to unbending zeal. Her example warns how conviction can harden into fanatical ruthlessness.",["class:Paladin"]="To paladins of the Silver Hand, Whitemane’s leadership shows how Lordaeron’s defenders were corrupted. They abandoned mercy and justice for indiscriminate purges.",["race:Undead"]="To the Forsaken, Whitemane embodies the Crusade’s refusal to distinguish mindless Scourge from free-willed undead. Her destruction is essential to the Undercity’s survival.",["faction:Alliance"]="Whitemane was once an Alliance citizen of Lordaeron. Her Crusade now attacks outsiders who approach its lands, forcing Southshore’s loyalists to face what their former kin have become."},kw={"cathedral","high inquisitor","raleigh the devout","renault mograine","sally whitemane","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:southshore","zone:undercity","npc:varimathras","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Sally Whitemane"}}
E["npc:scarlet-commander-mograine"] = {t="npc",n="Scarlet Commander Mograine",z="scarlet",s="Within the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Commander Mograine guards the Cathedral with the Scarlet Crusade. A zealous paladin, he faces efforts by the Horde and Alliance to disrupt the Crusade's threat to Tirisfal Glades and the lands around it.",h="Within the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Commander Mograine guards the Cathedral with the Scarlet Crusade.",sec={{t="Defender of the Chapel",b="At the heart of the Scarlet Monastery, Scarlet Commander Mograine leads the Scarlet Crusade garrison in the Crusader's Chapel. A devoted paladin, he strikes with holy power and shields himself. Those the Crusade judges corrupted or unclean meet his stunning blows.",sp=0},{t="A Miraculous Bond",b="High Inquisitor Whitemane fights beside Mograine in the chapel. When an attacking force brings him down, Whitemane comes from the rear sanctum. She incapacitates the intruders with the Holy Light and restores Mograine from death. Their attackers must then face both commanders at once.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where can Scarlet Commander Mograine be found?",a="Scarlet Commander Mograine waits before the altar in the Crusader's Chapel, inside the Cathedral wing of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"mograine location","where is mograine","scarlet monastery mograine room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Mograine's role in the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Mograine commands the Scarlet Crusade forces garrisoned at the Monastery. He leads its paladins and soldiers alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"who is commander mograine","mograine rank","what does mograine do"},it="identity"},{q="How does he fight?",a="Mograine fights at close range as a paladin. He stuns opponents with Hammer of Justice and strikes with Crusader Strikes. Retribution Aura protects him, and he uses Divine Shield when pressed.",al={"mograine abilities","mograine combat","how to fight mograine"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does High Inquisitor Whitemane revive him?",a="High Inquisitor Whitemane revives Mograine because they share a close bond and lead the Monastery together. When he falls, she puts their attackers to sleep with magic and raises him to full strength.",al={"whitemane res mograine","does mograine revive","resurrect mograine"},it="ties"},{q="Why are the Alliance and Horde fighting him?",a="The Scarlet Crusade sees outsiders, living or undead, as carriers of corruption. The Alliance and the Forsaken send champions against the Cathedral to kill its leaders and weaken the Crusade's fanatical presence in Lordaeron.",al={"why kill mograine","scarlet commander quest","in the name of the light"},it="conflict"},{q="Does Mograine heal himself during the encounter?",a="Yes. When pressed, Mograine can use Lay on Hands to restore himself to full health. High Inquisitor Whitemane also brings healing when she joins the battle.",al={"can mograine heal","mograine healing"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Scarlet Commander Mograine on?",a="Commander Mograine fights solely for the Scarlet Crusade. Though once drawn from Lordaeron's surviving defenders and the Knights of the Silver Hand, the Crusade now stands entirely isolated. Under Mograine's military command, they view all outsiders—Horde and Alliance alike—as plague-ridden filth and enemies of the Holy Light.",al={"who does mograine fight for","scarlet commander mograine faction","is mograine alliance"},it="side",add="a3e1ab86"},{q="Why is Scarlet Commander Mograine at the Monastery?",a="The Scarlet Monastery serves as a principal bastion of the Scarlet Crusade in Tirisfal Glades. Mograine holds the Crusader's Chapel within the Cathedral, directing the garrison's military defense alongside High Inquisitor Whitemane while guarding the heart of their holy fortress.",al={"why is mograine in scarlet monastery","mograine location reason","what is mograine doing here"},it="why_here",add="741d495f"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="Mograine shows how a paladin's vows of protection and righteousness can be twisted into ruthless zealotry.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Commander Mograine is the Scarlet Crusade's sharpest blade. His forces are near the Undercity and threaten Forsaken survival in Tirisfal.",["faction:Alliance"]="The Scarlet Crusade once shared common ground with the Alliance. Leaders in Southshore and Stormwind now see commanders like Mograine as fallen into violent madness."},kw={"cathedral","crusader's chapel","mograine","paladin","scarlet commander mograine","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:light"},src={"Scarlet Commander Mograine"}}
E["subzone:chamber-of-atonement"] = {t="subzone",n="Chamber of Atonement",z="scarlet",s="Captured undead and accused heretics face interrogation and torture in the Chamber of Atonement. At the entrance to the Scarlet Monastery's Graveyard wing, the hall opens onto the cloister where the Scarlet Crusade casts their remains.",h="Captured undead and accused heretics face interrogation and torture in the Chamber of Atonement.",sec={{t="A Hall of Agony",b="The Chamber of Atonement opens onto the Forlorn Cloister, where no peace or prayer waits. The Scarlet Crusade has filled this grand entry hall with racks, shackles, and burning braziers. Zealous inquisitors use them to force confessions and torment captives. They believe unholy beings deserve pain as penance, while cries echo and cruel taskmasters keep watch.",sp=0},{t="The Interrogator's Domain",b="Interrogator Vishas oversees the chamber. He takes pride in breaking anyone caught crossing the monastery's boundaries. The Forsaken captive Vorrel Sengutz has endured weeks of torment at his hands. Here, the Scarlet Crusade's campaign for purity has turned to sadism.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Chamber of Atonement used for?",a="In the monastery's Graveyard wing, the Scarlet Crusade uses the Chamber of Atonement to interrogate and torture captives. Forsaken and others it sees as enemies are questioned and tormented with brutal implements before their bodies are cast into the graveyard.",al={"chamber purpose","why are there torture devices here","what happens in chamber of atonement"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls this chamber?",a="Interrogator Vishas commands the chamber. The Scarlet Crusade torturer takes pleasure in his victims' suffering.",al={"who is the boss here","chamber of atonement leader","who runs the torture chamber"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where does this room lead?",a="The Chamber of Atonement opens directly into the Forlorn Cloister, at the outermost edge of the Graveyard wing. Fallen Crusaders and restless dead dwell in its open-air cemetery grounds.",al={"chamber exits","where does chamber of atonement go","next area after atonement"},it="place"},{q="Who is being held captive here?",a="Vorrel Sengutz, a Forsaken captive, has been imprisoned and tortured by Interrogator Vishas for weeks.",al={"who is prisoner here","vorrel sengutz","tortured prisoner"},it="target"},{q="What is the Chamber of Atonement?",a="The Chamber of Atonement is the outermost hall of the Graveyard wing within the Scarlet Monastery. Positioned directly before the Forlorn Cloister and the open cemetery grounds, it serves as a grim threshold where the Scarlet Crusade drags captives to endure brutal interrogations.",al={"what is chamber of atonement","chamber of atonement info","about chamber of atonement"},it="place",add="5cd82fbf"},{q="Is the Chamber of Atonement dangerous?",a="It is exceedingly dangerous. The chamber is manned by fanatical Scarlet torturers led by Interrogator Vishas, surrounded by gruesome implements of torment. Any intruders or perceived sympathizers of the undead are immediately set upon and subjected to the same merciless cruelty visited upon their prisoners.",al={"is chamber of atonement dangerous","chamber of atonement threats","how dangerous is chamber of atonement"},it="danger",add="f468ffff"},{q="Why is it called the Chamber of Atonement?",a="The Scarlet Crusade named the hall for their twisted belief that any being tainted by undeath or opposing their crusade must confess and pay for their sins through agony. To the inquisitors, suffering and torture under their blades are the only true paths to penance.",al={"why chamber of atonement","chamber of atonement name meaning","why is it called atonement"},it="name",add="1937bc67"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the Chamber of Atonement shows the Scarlet Crusade's cruelty toward your people. Captive Forsaken like Vorrel Sengutz are tortured here for existing.",["class:Priest"]="Here, the Scarlet Crusade's interrogators turn sacred discipline into physical torment. The chamber shows how far they have strayed from holy vows."},kw={"chamber of atonement","forlorn cloister","graveyard","interrogator vishas","scarlet monastery","torture","vorrel sengutz"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:interrogator-vishas","subzone:forlorn-cloister","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:forsaken"},src={"Chamber of Atonement"}}
E["subzone:crusader-s-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Crusader's Armory",z="scarlet",s="Munitions fill the Crusader's Armory in the Scarlet Monastery. Narrow halls hold gunpowder and cannonballs for the zealots guarding the way inward. A locked iron door bars the path to the Hall of Champions.",h="Munitions fill the Crusader's Armory in the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="Arsenal of Zeal",b="Between the Footman's Armory and the Hall of Champions, narrow stone corridors hold crates of gunpowder and stacks of cannonballs. Armed crusaders stand ready to turn back intruders. The Scarlet Crusade has made a fortress of a former monastic compound, filling every available hall with the tools of war. A heavy iron door, locked with the Scarlet Key, bars the way into the inner chambers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Crusader's Armory?",a="The Crusader's Armory holds ammunition in the passage between the Footman's Armory and the Hall of Champions, within the Scarlet Monastery's Armory wing.",al={"crusaders armory","what is crusaders armory","monastery armory room"},it="place"},{q="Why is the door at the end locked?",a="The locked door guards the passage to the Hall of Champions and the commander's quarters beyond. The Scarlet Crusade requires the Scarlet Key from the Monastery's Library wing to open it.",al={"locked door armory","how to open armory door","scarlet key armory"},gp=true},{q="Why are there so many cannonballs and gunpowder crates here?",a="The Scarlet Crusade stores cannonballs and gunpowder here for its cannons and explosive ordnance. Its active siege presence and artillery defenses across Tirisfal Glades need steady supplies for war against the Scourge and Forsaken.",al={"powder crates armory","cannons in monastery","why gunpowder"},it="purpose"},{q="Who guards this area?",a="Seasoned Scarlet Crusade soldiers guard the hall among the munitions, including footmen, crusaders, and archers. They stop invaders trying to push deeper into the complex.",al={"armory mobs","who is in crusaders armory"},it="residents"},{q="Is the Crusader's Armory dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The armory is packed with zealous Scarlet Crusade fighters who attack any intruder on sight, treating every outsider as an agent of corruption or the Scourge. Adding to the peril, the entire corridor is crammed with high explosives, including volatile powder kegs and artillery stockpiles ready for their relentless war in Tirisfal Glades.",al={"crusaders armory danger","is crusaders armory safe","crusader armory threats"},it="danger",add="2e345cd4"},{q="Why is it called the Crusader's Armory?",a="The chamber takes its name from the Scarlet Crusaders who garrison it and store their siege materiel within. Situated deep within the Scarlet Monastery's military wing past the Footman's Armory, it holds the cannon shot, gunpowder, and weapons designated for the Crusade's seasoned warriors as they prepare to assault the surrounding Plaguelands.",al={"why is it called crusaders armory","crusaders armory name origin","crusader armory meaning"},it="name",add="9c475e8e"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="For the Forsaken and the Horde, the explosive stores in the Crusader's Armory threaten Tirisfal Glades' borders and the gates of the Undercity.",["profession:Blacksmithing"]="The weapons and munitions stockpiled here show the high production value and military discipline of Lordaeron's former smiths, now given to zealous fanaticism."},kw={"armory","crusader's armory","gunpowder","hall of champions","scarlet key","scarlet monastery"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:hall-of-champions","zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Crusader's Armory"}}
E["subzone:forlorn-cloister"] = {t="subzone",n="Forlorn Cloister",z="scarlet",s="Among the tombs of Forlorn Cloister, the fallen dead rise, and Scarlet Crusaders burn their bodies to stop them.",h="Among the tombs of Forlorn Cloister, the fallen dead rise, and Scarlet Crusaders burn their bodies to stop...",sec={{t="A Consecration Consumed",b="You enter a graveyard where Scarlet Crusaders hurry between tombs with torches. They burn their fallen brothers, but the plague has already tainted the earth beneath them.\n\nOnce, priests and paladins of Lordaeron laid their honoured dead here in peace. Now spectres drift between the crypts, and corpses claw their way from the graves. The Crusaders keep watch, yet dark magic deep in the grounds still calls the dead to rise.",sp=0},{t="The Master of the Tombs",b="Bloodmage Thalnos commands the dead within the cloister. A skeletal sorcerer, he is another of the Monastery's tragedies, lost to undeath and hungry for vengeance. With dark magic, he binds the souls of the deceased and slaughters anyone who enters his blighted graveyard.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Forlorn Cloister located?",a="Forlorn Cloister occupies the outdoor graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery, in the northeastern corner of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"forlorn cloister location","where is cloister","graveyard wing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are the Scarlet Crusaders burning bodies here?",a="The Scarlet Crusade burns its fallen in a desperate effort to keep the Scourge plague from raising them. The cloister's soil is already tainted, and unburned bodies soon rise as mindless zombies.",al={"why burn corpses","burning bodies scarlet","what are crusaders doing"},it="purpose"},{q="Who rules over the Forlorn Cloister?",a="Bloodmage Thalnos rules the graveyard. The powerful undead spellcaster commands the wandering dead and attacks living intruders.",al={"cloister boss","who is in charge here","graveyard boss"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the graveyard haunted if the Scarlet Crusade holds the Monastery?",a="The Scarlet Crusaders have lost control of their cemetery despite their religious fervour. Necromantic energies sweeping through Lordaeron have stirred the buried dead, leaving the living garrison in a ceaseless fight against the spirits of their former peers.",al={"why are there ghosts","why undead in monastery","is graveyard scourge"}},{q="What is the Forlorn Cloister?",a="The Forlorn Cloister is the open-air graveyard wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Once a peaceful place of rest for the order's fallen, it has deteriorated into a desolate courtyard where earth and crypts crawl with restless dead. Even as the Scarlet Crusade fiercely defends the rest of the monastery, here they fight a desperate, unending skirmish simply to contain the horrors rising from the soil.",al={"what is forlorn cloister","forlorn cloister scarlet monastery","about forlorn cloister"},it="place",add="9a53d37e"},{q="Is the Forlorn Cloister dangerous?",a="The cloister is dangerous. Zealous Scarlet Crusaders burn bodies while restless wraiths and walking corpses wander among the tombstones. Deeper within dwells Bloodmage Thalnos, an undead mage who attacks intruders.",al={"is forlorn cloister dangerous","forlorn cloister threats","danger in forlorn cloister"},it="danger",add="a5f6d48a"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you see what happens when a holy sanctum falls to darkness. Sacred rites give way to frantic pyres, and tortured apparitions roam the grounds.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you may see a grim irony here. The zealous Crusaders brand all undead as monsters, yet cannot stop their own brothers from rising beneath their feet."},kw={"forlorn cloister","graveyard","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","thalnos","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Forlorn Cloister"}}
E["subzone:gallery-of-treasures"] = {t="subzone",n="Gallery of Treasures",z="scarlet",s="In the Scarlet Monastery, the Gallery of Treasures joins the Huntsman's Cloister to the Athenaeum. The Scarlet Crusade guards a corridor of Lordaeron's paintings, relics, and illuminated texts as it wages war against the undead.",h="In the Scarlet Monastery, the Gallery of Treasures joins the Huntsman's Cloister to the Athenaeum.",sec={{t="A Repository of Lost Heritage",b="Deep in the Library wing, the Gallery of Treasures runs from the Huntsman's Cloister kennels to the Athenaeum archives. Paintings and historical artifacts line the corridor. Small chambers hold books salvaged from across fallen Lordaeron.\n\nThe Scarlet Crusade calls these relics humanity's untainted legacy and has sworn to protect that heritage. Its zealots guard the passage against outsiders who enter their sanctuary.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Gallery of Treasures located?",a="The Gallery of Treasures lies inside the Library wing of the Scarlet Monastery. Just past the Huntsman's Cloister, the decorated passage leads to the Athenaeum.",al={"gallery location","where is gallery of treasures","how to find gallery of treasures"},it="place"},{q="What is kept in the Gallery of Treasures?",a="The Gallery holds preserved artwork, historical relics, illuminated texts, and paintings salvaged from ruined Lordaeron. They line the corridor and fill adjoining reading chambers.",al={"what is in gallery of treasures","gallery loot","gallery relics"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade collect these treasures?",a="The Scarlet Crusade sees itself as Lordaeron's true remnant. It gathers cultural works to preserve its homeland's memory and sacred heritage while purging what it considers taint.",al={"why do scarlet have treasures","crusade relics purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Who guards the gallery?",a="Scarlet Crusade zealots patrol the corridor, including defenders and initiates. They guard the path toward Arcanist Doan and the monastery's deeper archives.",al={"gallery mobs","who is in gallery of treasures"},it="residents"},{q="Is the Gallery of Treasures dangerous?",a="Yes, deeply so. The gallery is heavily guarded by zealous Scarlet Crusade defenders who view any outsider as an agent of corruption or the Scourge. Navigating its ornate halls means fighting past disciplined crusaders ready to slaughter trespassers on sight.",al={"is gallery of treasures dangerous","gallery of treasures danger","scarlet monastery gallery danger"},it="danger",add="a0f9e8c0"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you see artifacts and banners that recall the lost glory of the Silver Hand and fallen Lordaeron. Zealots hold them now, their righteous conviction turned to indiscriminate fanaticism.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see paintings and heirlooms that belonged to your Forsaken ancestors. Living crusaders guard them jealously as they seek to wipe out Lordaeron's former citizens."},kw={"athenaeum","gallery of treasures","library","lordaeron relics","paintings","scarlet monastery"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Gallery of Treasures"}}
E["subzone:grand-vestibule"] = {t="subzone",n="Grand Vestibule",z="scarlet",s="At the Grand Vestibule, Scarlet sentries guard the passage into the monastery’s inner halls. Crimson pillars and statues of fallen crusaders line the entrance.",h="At the Grand Vestibule, Scarlet sentries guard the passage into the monastery’s inner halls.",sec={{t="The Threshold of Zealotry",b="Past the Scarlet Monastery’s outer gates, you enter a marble hall lined with pillars and statues of armored champions. Scarlet sentries, disciples, and augurs patrol the flagstones. They strike down anyone who enters without the order’s crimson tabard. Here, the Crusade’s strict discipline meets its fervor.",sp=0},{t="A Contested Meeting Ground",b="Every intruder must cross the Grand Vestibule to reach the monastery’s guarded inner wings. Alliance champions sent north and Horde forces advancing from the nearby Undercity both face the Crusade’s defenders beneath its high arches. Beyond them lie the inner cloisters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Grand Vestibule?",a="The Grand Vestibule is an entrance chamber in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. It links the Scarlet Monastery’s outer courtyard to its four inner wings.",al={"what is this room","grand vestibule info","monastery entrance hall"},it="place"},{q="What enemies guard this area?",a="Scarlet Sentries, Scarlet Disciples, and Scarlet Augurs guard the chamber for the Scarlet Crusade and bar intruders.",al={"who patrols here","vestibule mobs","crusaders in vestibule"},it="threat"},{q="Why do the Alliance and Horde fight here?",a="Alliance champions enter the monastery to strike at the Crusade’s zealots, while the Horde seeks to secure Tirisfal Glades for the Forsaken. Both cross the same entrance hall, though no recorded battle between the factions took place there.",al={"pvp in vestibule","why are players fighting here","contested vestibule"},it="conflict"},{q="Whom do the statues in the vestibule depict?",a="The statues depict honored Scarlet Crusade warriors and heroes in heavy plate armor. They are symbols of the Crusade’s fight against the undead.",al={"who are the statues","vestibule statues","crusade monuments"}},{q="Who controls the Grand Vestibule?",a="The Scarlet Crusade holds total dominion over this grand entry chamber. Scarlet Augurs, Disciples, and Sentries stand watch among the towering pillars and carved statues, fiercely guarding the threshold to their inner sanctums against any whom they deem tainted or unworthy.",al={"who lives in grand vestibule","who runs grand vestibule","grand vestibule control"},it="residents",add="14cb93f7"},{q="Is the Grand Vestibule dangerous?",a="Extremely so. Scarlet Crusade defenders are posted throughout the hall, and they cut down intruders long before they can reach the monastery's inner wings.",al={"is grand vestibule safe","how dangerous is grand vestibule","grand vestibule danger"},it="danger",add="c059d7f1"},{q="Why is this hall called the Grand Vestibule?",a="A vestibule serves as an entrance hall or antechamber leading into a larger structure. As the outermost chamber of the Scarlet Monastery, its expansive architecture, towering colonnades, and ornate statues of crusade heroes make it truly grand in scale and purpose.",al={"why grand vestibule","grand vestibule name origin","meaning of grand vestibule"},it="name",add="38ab369b"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you face the living zealots threatening Forsaken sovereignty in Tirisfal from this grand entryway northeast of the Undercity.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you see how Lordaeron’s former holy sanctuaries have been corrupted. Devotion to the Light has turned to violent fanaticism."},kw={"entrance hall","grand vestibule","scarlet augur","scarlet disciple","scarlet monastery","scarlet sentry","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},src={"Grand Vestibule"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-champions"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Champions",z="scarlet",s="Within the Scarlet Monastery's armory wing, the Hall of Champions tests the Crusade's elite. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, leads its fiercest fighters from this inner sanctum.",h="Within the Scarlet Monastery's armory wing, the Hall of Champions tests the Crusade's elite.",sec={{t="Seat of the Scarlet Champion",b="Beyond the Footman's Armory, you come to the Hall of Champions at the heart of the monastery's armory wing. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, commands the Crusade's fiercest fighters here.\n\nScarlet trainees sharpen their resolve and skill for the Crusade's aim: to purge Lordaeron of all undead and outsiders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Hall of Champions?",a="The Hall of Champions is the inner sanctum of the monastery's armory and a proving ground for the Scarlet Crusade's elite. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, leads its fighters while trainees hone their skills for the war against the undead.",al={"what is hall of champions","hall of champions purpose","why are there statues here"},it="purpose"},{q="Who are the people immortalized in the statues?",a="No champions memorialized here are named in the records of this era. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, is the hall's best-known figure and guards the chamber.",al={"who are the statues","statue names hall of champions","monastery statues"},it="people"},{q="How does this hall differ from Stormwind's Champions' Hall?",a="Though their names are similar, the Hall of Champions lies deep inside the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades and honors Scarlet figures. Stormwind City's Champions' Hall is a military garrison reserved for Alliance officers and PvP quartermasters.",al={"is this stormwind pvp hall","hall of champions vs champions hall","pvp hall confusion"}},{q="What is the Hall of Champions?",a="The Hall of Champions is the inner sanctum of the Scarlet Monastery's armory wing, situated just beyond the Footman's Armory. It is the seat of Herod, the Scarlet Champion, where the Crusade's fiercest fighters stand ready against intruders.",al={"what is hall of champions","hall of champions scarlet"},it="place",add="c3492897"},{q="Who oversees the Hall of Champions?",a="Herod, the Scarlet Champion, occupies the Hall of Champions in the monastery's Armory. He is one of the Crusade's prominent leaders there.",al={"who runs hall of champions","who is in hall of champions","hall of champions boss"},it="residents",add="379bd11f"},{q="Is the Hall of Champions dangerous?",a="Yes. Herod and the Scarlet defenders are hostile to trespassers. Entering this chamber means confronting the Crusade within its own stronghold.",al={"is hall of champions safe","danger hall of champions"},it="danger",add="91532869"},{q="Why is it called the Hall of Champions?",a="The chamber takes its name from its role as the seat of the Crusade's champions, where Herod, the Scarlet Champion, holds sway over the order's elite fighters.",al={"why called hall of champions","name hall of champions"},it="name",add="9eb683e4"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="As a knight of the Holy Light, facing Herod, the Scarlet Champion, in his own hall reminds you that genuine virtue and faith can twist into zealotry.",["race:Human"]="As a human traveler from Lordaeron, you may recognize former defenders of the northern kingdoms among the Crusade's champions. They have thrown their lot in with the fanatical Crusade."},kw={"footman's armory","hall of champions","herod","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","subzone:champions-hall","subzone:hall-of-legends"},src={"Hall of Champions"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Armory",z="scarlet",s="Behind iron gates, recruits train and weapons are forged for the Scarlet Crusade in Scarlet Monastery Armory. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, commands the wing.",h="Behind iron gates, recruits train and weapons are forged for the Scarlet Crusade in Scarlet Monastery Armory.",sec={{t="The Foundry of Zeal",b="The Scarlet Monastery once sheltered Lordaeron's peaceful priesthood. After the Third War, the Crusade remade the Armory into a forge, a weapons depot, and a proving ground. Scarlet footmen, conjurers, and crusaders train in its open yards and deep halls. They mean to purge the Scourge and all they judge tainted. The wing is sealed from the Grand Vestibule. Only those bearing the Scarlet Key from the neighboring Library may enter.",sp=0},{t="The Hall of Champions",b="Towering statues of the Scarlet Crusade's heroes fill the Hall of Champions. Herod, the Scarlet Champion, oversees the hall. The brutal warrior is famed among the crusaders for his ferocity and whirling attacks, and trains new zealots himself. When battle presses him hard, his recruits rush into the chamber to fight and die for their champion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you get inside the Armory?",a="The Armory door in the Grand Vestibule is locked. You can retrieve the Scarlet Key from the chest behind Arcanist Doan in the Library's Athenaeum, or bring a rogue skilled enough to pick the lock.",al={"armory locked","how to unlock armory","scarlet key armory","open armory door"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Who leads the troops in the Armory?",a="Herod, the Scarlet Champion, commands the wing from the Hall of Champions. There he drills soldiers and puts recruits through fierce combat trials.",al={"armory boss","who is in charge of armory","who runs the armory","herod armory"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the purpose of this wing for the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Armory is the Scarlet Crusade's main arsenal and training ground. Its forges and weapon stores supply footmen and crusaders. Its outdoor yards prepare soldiers for dispatch across Tirisfal and the Plaguelands.",al={"why does armory exist","what do they do here","armory purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Whose statues are honored in the Hall of Champions?",a="The statues honor the Scarlet Crusade's most praised martyrs and heroes. Crusaders invoke their memory as they drill recruits for war against the undead.",al={"armory statues","hall of champions statues","statues in herod room"},it="fame"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Armory?",a="The Armory is a heavily fortified wing within the Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once dedicated to the peaceful worship and study of the Holy Light under Lordaeron's priesthood, it now serves as the training barracks, weapons depot, and assembly grounds for the Scarlet Crusade's militant zealots.",al={"what is the armory","scarlet monastery armory lore","about armory"},it="place",add="469efc8f"},{q="What happened to the Armory?",a="During the Third War, the Scourge decimated Lordaeron, sweeping through the region and transforming the peaceful center of learning into a desperate redoubt. Surviving clergy and soldiers radicalized into the Scarlet Crusade, arming themselves and fortifying the grounds into an unyielding bastion committed to exterminating anyone they suspect of harboring the plague.",al={"armory history","what happened at the armory","scarlet monastery armory background"},it="history",add="cd55d42c"},{q="Is the Armory dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The halls teem with fanatical crusaders, footmen, and battle-mages trained to kill on sight. The Crusade considers all outsiders potential carriers of the Scourge, meaning any intruder who enters the training grounds or halls faces disciplined, relentless soldiers fighting to the death.",al={"how dangerous is the armory","is armory safe","armory threat"},it="danger",add="edfdc72e"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you can see the Armory's hard lessons in mortal combat, from stances and disarms to Herod's renowned whirlwind technique.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face a Scarlet Crusade army gathering outside the gates of the Undercity. Raiding its weapons and killing its champion is vital to the Forsaken's survival."},kw={"armory","crusader's armory","footman's armory","hall of champions","herod","scarlet champion","scarlet key","scarlet monastery armory"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:herod","subzone:hall-of-champions","subzone:crusader-s-armory","subzone:grand-vestibule","topic:scarlet-crusade"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Armory"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Cathedral",z="scarlet",s="Within Scarlet Monastery Cathedral, the Crusade keeps its inner sanctum and command seat.",h="Within Scarlet Monastery Cathedral, the Crusade keeps its inner sanctum and command seat.",sec={{t="Sanctum of Zeal",b="After the Third War, hatred took hold of the Cathedral. The Scourge destroyed Lordaeron, and its surviving zealots turned the complex from a peaceful place of prayer and learning into a stronghold. Beyond the Chapel Gardens stands the grand Crusader's Chapel. There, priests and warriors gather in devotion to their cause. They see every outsider, whatever their race or faction, as a bearer of the undead plague, to be purged by blade and holy fire.",sp=0},{t="The High Inquisitor and Her Commander",b="Scarlet Commander Mograine directs the Cathedral's garrison with iron discipline. High Inquisitor Whitemane is the heart of its fanaticism and a formidable wielder of the Light. Her divine devotion lets her raise fallen champions in battle. Together, Whitemane and Mograine hold the inner chapel against anyone who breaches the monastery gates, keeping the Crusade's grip on northern Lordaeron deadly.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Cathedral used for?",a="The Cathedral holds the Scarlet Crusade's inner sanctum and sacred seat of power within the Monastery. Its leaders conduct religious services and direct military campaigns across Tirisfal Glades.",al={"cathedral purpose","why visit cathedral","what is this place"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the Scarlet Crusade here?",a="Scarlet Commander Mograine commands the garrison, while High Inquisitor Whitemane holds spiritual authority as a formidable, zealous priestess.",al={"who is the boss here","cathedral bosses","whitemane mograine"},it="leader"},{q="Why is the door to the Cathedral locked?",a="Heavy gates bar intruders from the Cathedral's inner sanctum. Entry requires the Scarlet Key, kept under guard in the Monastery's Library wing.",al={"cathedral locked","how to open cathedral","where is the key"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Crusaders attacking other living humans?",a="The Scourge destroyed Lordaeron, and the Crusade now sees every outsider as a carrier of undeath. Its zealots shun other factions and execute anyone who approaches their fortresses.",al={"why attack alliance","scarlet crusade evil","why crusade hostile"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral?",a="The Cathedral is the central, crowning wing of the Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once a revered sanctuary of Lordaeron's priesthood dedicated to learning and spiritual enlightenment, it now serves as the sanctum sanctorum and command seat for the zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.",al={"what is cathedral","scarlet cathedral","cathedral wing"},it="place",add="9962382e"},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral?",a="Before the Third War, this peaceful monastery stood as a proud bastion of Lordaeron's Holy Light, devoted to study and healing. When the Scourge tore through the kingdom, surviving defenders fortified the holy site, transforming its tranquil halls and courtyards into a heavily armed fortress driven by paranoia and fanatical hatred.",al={"cathedral history","what happened here","monastery past"},it="history",add="d9fd8161"},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Cathedral dangerous?",a="It is by far the most perilous quarter of the monastery. Beyond its courtyard lies a grand chapel crammed with elite crusaders, devoted abbots, and deadly sorcerers. Its defenders fight with zealous fury, and intruders face the combined might of Commander Mograine and the formidable High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"cathedral danger","is it safe here","how dangerous is cathedral"},it="danger",add="09ab4f6a"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For the Alliance, the Crusade twists the Holy Light and Lordaeron's proud heritage into something corrupt. Commanders in Southshore send champions to end its madness.",["faction:Horde"]="The Cathedral lies dangerously close to the Undercity. Its zealots seek to exterminate the Forsaken and any Horde allies who stand with them."},kw={"cathedral","chapel gardens","crusader's chapel","high inquisitor","mograine","scarlet monastery","whitemane"},rel={"zone:scarlet","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","subzone:grand-vestibule","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:lordaeron","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge","topic:light"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Cathedral"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Graveyard",z="scarlet",s="Undead haunt Scarlet Monastery Graveyard in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Lordaeron's clergy and nobility once rested here in peace, but neglect and Bloodmage Thalnos's corrupted magic now trouble the burial wing.",h="Undead haunt Scarlet Monastery Graveyard in northeastern Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Before the Third War, Lordaeron's priests rested in peace in this cloistered cemetery. When the Scarlet Crusade fortified the monastery against the undead, its fanatical watch left the crypts uncleansed. Now the Graveyard lies neglected and haunted. Lingering spirits, restless corpses, and shambling horrors wander the Chamber of Atonement and the mist-covered Forlorn Cloister. Beneath the Crusade's uncaring gaze, the dead suffer endless torment instead of hallowed rest.",sp=0},{t="Corruption from Within",b="At the rear of the grounds, Honor's Tomb holds Bloodmage Thalnos, who mocks the Crusade's dogma. No record tells who he was in life. The plague of undeath claimed him, and he rose as a skeletal horror wielding shadow bolts and fire. The crusaders above preach the total extermination of the undead plague. Yet a rotting, fallen sorcerer remains in their consecrated soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are there undead inside a Scarlet Crusade stronghold?",a="The Crusade's leadership is consumed by fanaticism. It sends crusaders outward to slaughter living outsiders and wage war in Tirisfal. Meanwhile, the monastery's crypts and burial plots lie utterly neglected, allowing dormant plague remnants and restless spirits of dead clergy to rise unchecked.",al={"why undead in sm gy","undead in scarlet monastery","why are there ghosts here"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Bloodmage Thalnos?",a="No record tells who Thalnos was in life. The plague of undeath claimed him, and he rose as a skeletal spellcaster who rules the desecrated crypts of Honor's Tomb.",al={"thalnos lore","who is bloodmage thalnos","graveyard boss"},it="identity"},{q="Where is the Graveyard wing located inside the monastery?",a="Enter the Grand Vestibule of the Scarlet Monastery and take the leftmost portal to reach the Graveyard. It needs no key, unlike the Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"where is sm gy","how to find graveyard wing","which door is graveyard"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Forlorn Cloister?",a="The Forlorn Cloister is an open-air garden and cemetery between the entrance crypts and Honor's Tomb. Tombstones, roaming ghouls, and damp earth rich in Grave Moss fill the grounds.",al={"forlorn cloister","graveyard courtyard"},it="place"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="It is the leftmost wing of the Scarlet Monastery complex in northeastern Tirisfal Glades. Once serving as the burial grounds and crypts for Lordaeron's holy order, it has fallen into corruption and neglect, filled with tombs, mausoleums, and the unquiet dead.",al={"what is the graveyard","graveyard wing","scarlet graveyard"},it="place",add="2ee90fec"},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="Originally a quiet resting place for honored priests and champions of Lordaeron, the grounds fell under the control of the Scarlet Crusade when the monastery was fortified against the Scourge. Rather than finding peaceful rest, the bodies buried here began to rise as undead, leaving the Crusade to wall off the blighted burial grounds.",al={"history of the graveyard","what happened here","graveyard origin"},it="history",add="d7efe218"},{q="Who controls the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="While the Crusade claims the wider monastery complex, the Graveyard wing itself is largely abandoned to the restless undead. The fallen mage Thalnos, corrupted into a bloodthirsty, skeletal spellcaster, lords over the innermost tomb alongside scattered ghouls, ghosts, and wandering dead.",al={"who runs the graveyard","who is in charge here","graveyard leader"},it="residents",add="35b34413"},{q="Why is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard abandoned and ruined?",a="The Crusade's fanatical holy power could not prevent the Scourge's plague from desecrating their dead. Unable to cleanse the rising corpses completely, the living crusaders withdrew to their fortified chapels and armories, leaving the burial grounds overgrown and overrun by reanimated corpses.",al={"why is the graveyard ruined","why is it abandoned","why neglected"},it="ruin",add="c4dc5010"},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard dangerous?",a="Yes. While less organized than the martial forces occupying the other monastery wings, the Graveyard is filled with aggressive undead, malicious spirits, and dark spellcasters like Bloodmage Thalnos who mercilessly assault any living intruders who trespass upon the tombs.",al={"is the graveyard dangerous","danger in the graveyard","how dangerous is the graveyard"},it="danger",add="2daa3a11"},{q="Why is it called the Scarlet Monastery Graveyard?",a="It serves as the dedicated burial grounds and cemetery of the Scarlet Monastery. It houses ancient crypts, mausoleums like Honor's Tomb, and the Forlorn Cloister where Lordaeron's holy defenders were traditionally laid to rest.",al={"why is it called the graveyard","graveyard name","why scarlet monastery graveyard"},it="name",add="cfbfb429"}},ang={["profession:Herbalism"]="The damp, defiled soil of the Forlorn Cloister is one of northern Lordaeron's most reliable places to gather Grave Moss.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you may see the Graveyard as grim proof of the Crusade's hypocrisy. Its zealots condemn the Forsaken while an undead bloodmage rots in their basement."},kw={"chamber of atonement","forlorn cloister","grave moss","graveyard","honor's tomb","scarlet monastery","thalnos"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:grand-vestibule","npc:bloodmage-thalnos","subzone:forlorn-cloister","subzone:chamber-of-atonement","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:scourge"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Graveyard"}}
E["subzone:scarlet-monastery-library"] = {t="subzone",n="Scarlet Monastery Library",z="scarlet",s="In Tirisfal Glades, scholars and mages seek Lordaeron's old religious and arcane records in the Scarlet Monastery Library. Crusade zealots and battle hounds patrol its halls.",h="In Tirisfal Glades, scholars and mages seek Lordaeron's old religious and arcane records in the Scarlet...",sec={{t="Archives of Lordaeron",b="Before the Third War, Lordaeron's priesthood came to the monastery to study. Its eastern cloisters held religious writings, histories, and arcane treatises. Then the Scarlet Crusade fortified the monastery against the Scourge. They kept the archives and armed the quiet halls.\n\nNow beastmasters send tracking hounds through the courtyards, while battle-mages patrol the shelves. They guard the Compendium of the Fallen and ancient Titan research from outsiders.",sp=0},{t="Guardians of the Athenaeum",b="Houndmaster Loksey guards the Huntsman's Cloister with trained hounds. They sniff out anyone seeking passage to the inner chambers. Beyond the Gallery of Treasures, Arcanist Doan watches over the Athenaeum.\n\nA formidable mage, Doan wields devastating fire and protective sorcery. Doan studies alone and fiercely defends the Crusade's hoarded knowledge from anyone who enters the heart of the complex.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Library within the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Enter the Grand Vestibule of the Scarlet Monastery in Tirisfal Glades, then take the rightmost portal to reach the Library wing.",al={"library entrance","which door is library","how to find library wing"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are adventurers sent to the Library?",a="Scholars, priests, and mages from the Alliance and Horde seek precious texts kept in the Library. They seek the Compendium of the Fallen, Titan lore sought by Ironforge historians, and ancient magical manuals for rising arcanists.",al={"why go to library","library quests","what is in the library"},it="purpose"},{q="Who rules the Library wing?",a="Arcanist Doan presides over the Library's inner sanctuary, the Athenaeum. Houndmaster Loksey and his tracking beasts guard the outer courtyard.",al={"library boss","who is in charge of the library","who leads the library"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the Scarlet Key found here?",a="A lockbox in Arcanist Doan's Athenaeum holds the Scarlet Key. It opens the heavy iron doors to the monastery's Armory and Cathedral wings.",al={"doan key","scarlet key drop","where is scarlet key"},it="item"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Library?",a="The Library is the right-most wing of the sprawling Scarlet Monastery complex in Tirisfal Glades. Once a quiet center for study and clerical enlightenment in Lordaeron, it now houses the Scarlet Crusade's collected lore, military treasures, and hound kennels, divided into the Huntsman's Cloister, the Gallery of Treasures, and the Athenaeum.",al={"what is the library","scarlet library wing","monastery library overview"},it="place",add="10860e43"},{q="What happened to the Scarlet Monastery Library?",a="The Library originally stood as part of a proud bastion of Lordaeron's priesthood, dedicated to learning, theological study, and enlightenment. When the undead Scourge tore through the kingdom in the Third War, surviving human zealots fortified the entire complex. They converted the peaceful repository of books and holy knowledge into an armed redoubt of the fanatical Scarlet Crusade.",al={"history of scarlet monastery library","library past","what happened here"},it="history",add="05144c18"},{q="Is the Scarlet Monastery Library dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The Library is garrisoned by zealous Scarlet soldiers, priests, and battle mages who view all outsiders as carriers of the Scourge plague to be eradicated on sight. Intruders must fight through trained attack hounds commanded by Houndmaster Loksey before facing the lethal sorcery of Arcanist Doan in the inner Athenaeum.",al={"is scarlet monastery library dangerous","library threats","how dangerous is the library"},it="danger",add="a62144f3"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you can seek ancient rituals of power in the Athenaeum. There, you can test your mettle against Arcanist Doan's destructive sorcery.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can seek the Library's sacred records of Lordaeron's fallen heroes and Titan histories. Ironforge's Hall of Explorers is desperate to recover them from Crusader hands."},kw={"arcanist doan","athenaeum","compendium of the fallen","houndmaster loksey","library","scarlet key","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades"},rel={"zone:scarlet","subzone:grand-vestibule","npc:arcanist-doan","npc:houndmaster-loksey","topic:scarlet-crusade","quest:1152","quest:1950"},src={"Scarlet Monastery Library"}}
E["subzone:terrace-of-repose"] = {t="subzone",n="Terrace of Repose",z="scarlet",s="At the Scarlet Monastery, the Terrace of Repose remains green and clear amid Tirisfal Glades. The Scarlet Crusade tends this courtyard garden, untouched by the Plague of Undeath.",h="At the Scarlet Monastery, the Terrace of Repose remains green and clear amid Tirisfal Glades.",sec={{t="An Oasis in the Blight",b="Just north of the Scarlet Monastery's grand entrance, the Terrace of Repose is a green garden amid the blight. Beyond its hedges, grey mist hangs over Tirisfal Glades, where the soil is corrupt and the bogs lie stagnant. Here, a fountain runs with fresh, uncontaminated water, and the Scarlet Crusade tends the garden. Its zealots take these grounds as proof of their divine righteousness and purity. They believe holy devotion can ward off the Scourge's corruption.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the grass and water clean here when Tirisfal is dead?",a="The Plague of Undeath has not reached the Terrace of Repose. The Scarlet Crusade keeps its soil, thriving hedges, and clear water free of the surrounding rot through constant vigilance and perhaps fierce devotion to the Holy Light.",al={"why is it green here","clean water scarlet monastery","terrace of repose uncorrupted"},it="place"},{q="Where exactly is the Terrace of Repose located?",a="The Terrace of Repose lies just outside the Scarlet Monastery's entrance grounds, in the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades.",al={"where is terrace of repose","terrace of repose location","monastery garden entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What do the Crusaders use the terrace for?",a="The Crusaders use the terrace as an approach to their fortified monastery and as a quiet sanctuary on uncorrupted earth. They can rest and reflect there, and see an idealized glimpse of Lordaeron as it stood before the Third War.",al={"scarlet crusade garden use","purpose of terrace of repose"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Terrace of Repose?",a="The Terrace of Repose is a serene courtyard situated just north of the Scarlet Monastery's main entrance. Kept under close guard by the Scarlet Crusade, it stands out as one of the few pristine spots left in northern Lordaeron, boasting manicured green hedges and fresh, flowing water untouched by the Scourge's rot.",al={"what is terrace of repose","terrace of repose scarlet monastery","about terrace of repose"},it="place",add="f618a338"},{q="Who controls the Terrace of Repose?",a="The Scarlet Crusade maintains and controls the terrace. Positioned right outside their sprawling monastery stronghold, the area serves as an outdoor retreat and defensible garden tended by Crusader sentries and clergy determined to preserve a corner of Lordaeron as it existed before the fall.",al={"who lives at terrace of repose","who controls terrace of repose","terrace of repose faction"},it="residents",add="310f02b5"},{q="Is the Terrace of Repose dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous to anyone outside the Scarlet Crusade. The terrace is heavily patrolled by zealous Crusaders who attack any intruders on sight, whether you are Forsaken, Horde, or unaligned travelers venturing too close to the monastery gates.",al={"is terrace of repose dangerous","terrace of repose threats","can i visit terrace of repose"},it="danger",add="538b338a"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you see greenery tended by mortal enemies who wish to cleanse Lordaeron of your kind. The living world rejects you, and the terrace is a bitter reminder of that rejection.",["class:Paladin"]="As a paladin, you can see living plants and clean water in Tirisfal as proof that the land can heal. Unyielding fanatics tend the grounds now."},kw={"fountain","hedges","plague of undeath","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","terrace of repose","tirisfal glades","uncorrupted"},rel={"zone:scarlet","topic:scarlet-crusade","zone:tirisfal","topic:plague-of-undeath","topic:lordaeron"},src={"Terrace of Repose"}}
E["subzone:whispering-gardens"] = {t="subzone",n="Whispering Gardens",z="scarlet",s="In northeastern Tirisfal, the Whispering Gardens lie on the hillside south of the Scarlet Monastery. Early crusade defenders fought a host of the Scourge here. Now Scarlet crusaders patrol the overgrown paths, where faint voices linger.",h="In northeastern Tirisfal, the Whispering Gardens lie on the hillside south of the Scarlet Monastery.",sec={{t="A Battle Echoing in the Mist",b="Before the Scarlet Crusade withdrew behind the Monastery walls, the Whispering Gardens saw fierce fighting. Undead pressed across the terraces, and countless lives were lost on both sides.\n\nAt twilight, travelers crossing the gardens report soft murmurings on the wind. Many believe these are echoes of the soldiers and priests who died defending the holy grounds.",sp=0},{t="Crusader Outpost",b="The Scarlet Crusade keeps watch over the Whispering Gardens. Scouts, magicians, and preservers guard the trails against intruders from the lower glades.\n\nFor zealots in the nearby monastery, the overgrown steps guard their approach. They also recall the unceasing war against the undead.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where are the Whispering Gardens located?",a="The Whispering Gardens cover the hillside just south of the Scarlet Monastery in northeastern Tirisfal Glades.",al={"whispering gardens location","where is whispering gardens","how to get to whispering gardens"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are they called the Whispering Gardens?",a="The name comes from faint murmurs heard in the twilight air. They are said to be lingering voices of defenders and undead who fell in a bloody battle on the slopes.",al={"why is it called whispering gardens","what are the whispers","whispering gardens name"},it="name"},{q="What battle took place here?",a="An invading Scourge army fought the early forces that became the Scarlet Crusade. Many died before the Scourge was stopped outside the monastery.",al={"battle of whispering gardens","what happened at whispering gardens"},it="history"},{q="Who controls the gardens now?",a="The Scarlet Crusade controls the gardens. Its scouts, preservers, and magicians patrol the terraces and guard the southern approach to their stronghold.",al={"who lives in whispering gardens","monsters in whispering gardens"},it="residents"},{q="What are the Whispering Gardens?",a="The Whispering Gardens are a somber hillside terrace situated in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, just south of the entrance to the Scarlet Monastery. Once peaceful grounds, the terrace now serves as an outer defensive post and staging ground for the zealous forces of the Scarlet Crusade overlooking the surrounding glades.",al={"what is whispering gardens","whispering gardens lore","what are whispering gardens"},it="place",add="3774f1a6"},{q="How dangerous are the Whispering Gardens?",a="They are extremely hazardous to any outsider. The Scarlet Crusade keeps an active guard throughout the terrace, stationing magicians, preservers, and scouts across the paths. Driven by fanatic paranoia, they execute anyone not sworn to their cause on sight, treating all outsiders as carriers of the undead taint.",al={"is whispering gardens dangerous","whispering gardens danger","threats in whispering gardens"},it="danger",add="7713d5ca"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the gardens hold a fanatical Scarlet presence on Tirisfal's doorstep. Echoes of the war that doomed Lordaeron linger there.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you can sense spiritual traces of holy defenders who died violently against the Scourge. Their souls remain bound to the winds."},kw={"scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","scourge","tirisfal glades","whispering gardens","whispers"},rel={"zone:scarlet","zone:tirisfal","topic:scarlet-crusade","topic:scourge"},src={"Whispering Gardens"}}
E["zone:scarlet"] = {t="dungeon",n="Scarlet Monastery",z="scarlet",s="In the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Monastery shelters the Scarlet Crusade behind fortified walls. Once a peaceful sanctuary and a center of learning for the Church of the Holy Light, it now holds four wings where zealots train, torture captives, and wage war on outsiders.",h="In the northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, Scarlet Monastery shelters the Scarlet Crusade behind fortified...",sec={{t="A Fallen Sanctuary",b="Before the Third War, the Scarlet Monastery was a proud seat of Lordaeron's priesthood, devoted to learning and enlightenment. Then the Scourge devastated the land. The surviving crusaders cleared the halls of undead and spiders, and made the archives and courtyards a fortified garrison.\n\nGrief and fear hardened into suspicion. The Scarlet Crusade came to see every outsider as a carrier of the plague, living or undead, human or otherwise. In their eyes, such foes must be cleansed with fire.",sp=0},{t="The Four Wings",b="Beyond the Grand Vestibule lie four wings. In the Graveyard, fallen crusaders rise as undead abominations, while torturers force confessions from prisoners. The Library holds theological and historical works, guarded by renegade mage Arcanist Doan and his hounds.\n\nIn the Armory, weaponmasters such as Herod train recruits to fight as disciplined warriors. Deep within the stronghold lies the Cathedral, the Crusade's heart. There, its leaders direct their campaign across the blighted north.",sp=0},{t="The Fall of the High Inquisitor",b="Scarlet Commander Mograine commands the Cathedral's inner sanctum beside the monastery's true master, High Inquisitor Whitemane. Whitemane channels the Holy Light and can raise fallen champions. To her devotees, that power makes the garrison seem invincible.\n\nDefeating Whitemane strikes at the Crusade's command in Tirisfal Glades. It breaks the aura of divine authority behind the monastery's zealotry. The Crusade's leaders are mortal, and its campaign against the Forsaken and neighboring lands is badly weakened.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the Scarlet Crusade hostile to living Alliance adventurers?",a="The Scarlet Crusade has fallen into madness and paranoia. Its members see anyone without a crimson tabard as a possible carrier of the Scourge plague. They make no distinction between friend and foe, believing every outsider tainted and in need of purging before spreading corruption.",al={"why do scarlets attack humans","scarlet crusade hostile alliance","why are they mad"},it="hostile"},{q="What happens when you defeat High Inquisitor Whitemane?",a="Defeating High Inquisitor Whitemane deals a severe blow to the Scarlet Crusade's western leadership. As the monastery's spiritual leader, she raises the fallen and keeps Commander Mograine fighting at her side. Her death leaves the garrison disordered and weakens its threat to the surrounding region.",al={"what does killing whitemane mean","whitemane defeated lore","cathedral ending"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Scarlet Key and where is it found?",a="Arcanist Doan keeps the Scarlet Key in his strongbox, deep in the Library wing behind his study. The key opens the outer gates of both the Armory and the Cathedral wings.",al={"where is scarlet key","how to unlock armory and cathedral","monastery key"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why is Arcanist Doan in the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Arcanist Doan is a powerful human mage who serves the Scarlet Crusade. He believes arcane magic is needed to cleanse the Scourge from Lordaeron. In his study, he guards the monastery's Library and the Scarlet Key.",al={"who is arcanist doan","doan lore","mage in library"},it="identity"},{q="Who was Alexandros Mograine and how is he connected here?",a="Alexandros Mograine, the famed Ashbringer, was a legendary paladin of the Silver Hand and one of the Scarlet Crusade's founders. He founded it alongside High General Abbendis and Grand Inquisitor Isillien. His son Renault now commands the Cathedral with High Inquisitor Whitemane.",al={"mograine monastery history","ashbringer monastery","renault mograine father"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What makes the Graveyard wing so different from the rest of the monastery?",a="The Graveyard reveals the monastery's fanaticism in a harsher light. Interrogator Vishas runs its torture chambers. In neglected crypts, fallen casters such as Bloodmage Thalnos harvest or manipulate the restless dead.",al={"why is graveyard undead","thalnos lore","interrogator vishas"},it="place"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Perched in northeastern Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery is a fortified sanctuary and the principal bastion of the Scarlet Crusade in the region. Once a peaceful cathedral complex devoted to the Holy Light and clerical learning, the stronghold has been converted into a heavily armed headquarters, training ground, and ideological redoubt for the Crusade's zealous campaign against undeath.",al={"what is scarlet monastery","scarlet monastery lore","about scarlet monastery"},it="place",add="3ffc247b",nx={8}},{q="Was the Scarlet Monastery always theirs?",a="No. Before the fall of Lordaeron, it was known simply as the Old Monastery. Originally patronized by the noble House of Godwyn, it served as an archbishopric seat and seminary under Archbishop Alonsus Faol. Following the devastation of the Third War, surviving paladins reclaimed its halls from lingering Scourge infestations and renamed it the Scarlet Monastery.",al={"was scarlet monastery always crusade","history of scarlet monastery","who used to own scarlet monastery"},it="history",add="fd7417a7",nx={9}},{q="Who built the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The Old Monastery was constructed as a sanctuary of the Church of the Holy Light under the sponsorship of the noble House of Godwyn. Its libraries and archives were curated for generations by archivists like Blake Godwyn, standing as a proud center of Lordaeron's priesthood and paladin training until the kingdom's collapse.",al={"who built the monastery","origins of the monastery"},it="origin",add="e7b85043"},{q="Who are the Scarlet Crusade?",a="The Scarlet Crusade is a fanatical military order of human holy warriors and priests formed from remnants of the Knights of the Silver Hand. Consumed by grief and hatred following the Scourging of Lordaeron, they have committed themselves entirely to eradicating the undead, enforcing their mission with extreme ruthlessness and paranoia.",al={"who are scarlet crusade","what is the scarlet crusade","scarlet crusade lore"},it="threat",add="0c05301c",nx={11}},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade human?",a="Yes, their ranks consist entirely of humans from the fallen realm of Lordaeron. They harbor fierce intolerance toward all non-human races, regardless of alliance or former ties, deeming outsiders unworthy or inherently tainted by the plague.",al={"are scarlet crusade only human","crusade race","is scarlet crusade human"},it="people",add="b0ef06b1"},{q="Why am I attacking a church full of paladins?",a="Though they wear the trappings of holy orders and wield the Light, the Monastery's commanders have descended into violent extremism. Whether you answer the call of Raleigh the Devout to cleanse the order's corrupted leadership, or strike on behalf of Varimathras in the Undercity to neutralize an aggressive neighbor on his doorstep, you are there to break their military power.",al={"why attack scarlet monastery","why kill paladins here","reason to fight scarlet monastery"},it="purpose",add="1402011d",nx={13,14}},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade actually evil?",a="They began with a noble cause—purging Lordaeron of the undead Scourge. However, trauma and paranoia have warped their purpose entirely. They now torture innocent travelers, brand any outsider as plagued, and slaughter anyone not bearing their tabard, losing all moral sanity in the pursuit of purification.",al={"is scarlet crusade evil","are they bad guys","are crusaders evil"},it="motive",add="18e8d4ac"},{q="Does the Alliance support the Scarlet Crusade?",a="Not officially. While some in Stormwind may harbor sympathy for Lordaeron's surviving holy warriors, the Crusade's indiscriminate hostility has severed formal ties. Adventurers and Alliance figures like Raleigh the Devout view their current commanders as mad zealots whose atrocities stain the honor of the Light.",al={"does alliance support crusade","is scarlet crusade alliance","alliance ties to scarlet crusade"},it="allies",add="fe2faadd"},{q="Who is in charge of the Scarlet Monastery?",a="The stronghold's military garrison answers to Scarlet Commander Renault Mograine, who commands a devoted force of warriors. However, the true spiritual and doctrinal master of the complex is High Inquisitor Whitemane, a powerful priestess capable of reviving the fallen to fight in her name.",al={"who leads scarlet monastery","who runs the monastery","scarlet monastery leader"},it="in_charge",add="fbd0569e",nx={16}},{q="Is the leader of the Monastery inside the Cathedral?",a="Yes. Both Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane reside within the Crusader's Chapel deep inside the Cathedral wing, guarded by an inner retinue of zealous defenders.",al={"where is whitemane","is whitemane in cathedral","cathedral boss location"},it="place",add="ae07147f"},{q="Why does the Scarlet Crusade hate the Forsaken so much?",a="To the Crusade, all undead are abominations born of the plague that obliterated their families and homeland. They make no distinction between the mindless minions of the Scourge and the free-willed Forsaken occupying Capital City; both are seen as rotting usurpers that must be utterly cleansed in holy fire.",al={"crusade vs forsaken","why crusade hates undead","scarlet crusade forsaken feud"},it="history",add="11700a05",nx={18}},{q="Were the Scarlet Crusaders and the Forsaken the same people once?",a="Yes. Most Crusaders and Forsaken were citizens, soldiers, or priests of the Kingdom of Lordaeron before the Third War. When the plague swept through, those who died and rose again became the undead, while the traumatized living fled or rallied together, turning former neighbors and kin into bitter, sworn enemies.",al={"did crusaders and forsaken know each other","were they both lordaeron citizens","lordaeron remnants"},it="origin",add="38169c8a"},{q="Where did the Scarlet Crusade come from?",a="The Crusade arose from the surviving Knights of the Silver Hand and Lordaeron soldiers led by Highlord Alexandros Mograine and General Abbendis. Overwhelmed by the loss of their kingdom, the surviving leaders splintered: those advocating relentless, uncompromising zealotry formed the Scarlet Crusade, while moderates split away to found the Argent Dawn.",al={"origin of scarlet crusade","how was scarlet crusade founded","who started scarlet crusade"},it="history",add="80c0e472",nx={20}},{q="What was the Silver Hand?",a="The Knights of the Silver Hand were the legendary holy order of paladins founded during the Second War by Archbishop Alonsus Faol and Uther the Lightbringer. They served as the frontline champions of the Alliance and Lordaeron until Prince Arthas shattered their ranks during the Scourge's invasion.",al={"what were the silver hand","knights of the silver hand","silver hand paladins"},it="history",add="c4a70323"},{q="Why do the Scarlet Crusade kill living humans too?",a="Deep paranoia has eroded the Crusade's grip on reality. They believe that any outsider could be a covert carrier of the undead plague. Anyone not wearing their uniform and submitting to their rigid authority is branded corrupted and sentenced to torture or death.",al={"why attack living humans","crusade kills humans","why do they kill their own kind"},it="threat",add="d5472427"},{q="Are the Scarlet Crusade a threat to Stormwind?",a="Not directly in terms of geographic conquest, as their efforts are anchored in the northern ruins of Lordaeron. However, their madness and willingness to murder any traveler makes them an active menace to Alliance citizens, ambassadors, and adventurers venturing anywhere near their territories.",al={"is scarlet crusade a threat to alliance","crusade vs stormwind","threat of scarlet crusade"},it="threat",add="b6568619"},{q="Why does everyone want me to go into the Scarlet Monastery?",a="Both factions have vital stakes in Tirisfal Glades. The Forsaken cannot tolerate a heavily armed zealot fortress right outside their capital, while Alliance figures seek to recover sacred texts, quell dangerous renegades, and bring justice to leadership gone mad.",al={"why am i sent to scarlet monastery","who wants the monastery dead","scarlet monastery quests reason"},it="why_me",add="6889160e"},{q="What is the Scarlet Monastery Library for?",a="The Library, which includes the Athenaeum and Gallery of Treasures, houses ancient Lordaeron scriptures, historical records, and arcane lore. It serves as both an intellectual archive and a secluded research sanctuary presided over by Arcanist Doan.",al={"library wing purpose","what are they doing in the library","scarlet monastery athenaeum"},it="place",add="0c6b4a7d"},{q="What are the Armory and Cathedral wings used for?",a="The Armory acts as the Crusade's martial heart, housing training grounds, barracks, and weapon caches overseen by Herod the Scarlet Champion. The Cathedral stands as the supreme spiritual sanctuary and command post, where Mograine drills elite troops and Whitemane delivers sermons and coordinates the Crusade's presence in Tirisfal.",al={"what are armory and cathedral for","purpose of armory sm","cathedral sm purpose"},it="place",add="29dc31ee"},{q="How did I end up in Scarlet Monastery?",a="You traveled to the far northeastern hills of Tirisfal Glades, pushing through the misty glades to the fortified seat of the Scarlet Crusade. Whether you crept up from the Undercity under orders from the Horde to dismantle a zealot threat on their doorstep, or marched north from Hillsbrad Foothills answering the call of disillusioned crusaders seeking to purge the Monastery's fanatical leadership, the path inevitably brought you before this heavily guarded complex.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to scarlet monastery","why did i come here"},it="arrival",add="f04a1b7f"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Scarlet Monastery?",a="You are here to breach the Crusade's four wings and break their hold over the region. Depending on who sent you, you may be hunting down fallen leadership like Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane, uncovering lost tomes and lore within the library, gathering hearts of zeal for the Royal Apothecary Society, or recovering holy artifacts and slaying corrupted leaders who brand anyone outside their ranks as plagued undead.",al={"what am i doing here","why am i here","what is my mission here"},it="purpose",add="be779d1d"}},ang={["class:Paladin"]="The Scarlet Monastery was once a sacred seat of Lordaeron's priesthood and a center of learning. Its fall to crimson zealotry shows how devotion can curdle into madness.",["class:Priest"]="The Scarlet Monastery began as a seat of the Church of the Holy Light. Its grand chapels show holy power wielded by mortals twisted by hatred and vengeance.",["race:Undead"]="On the border of Tirisfal Glades, the Scarlet Monastery threatens the Forsaken. Its spies reach Deathknell, and its dungeons hold captured undead who are tortured.",["class:Mage"]="The Library wing holds rare historical and theological works. Arcanist Doan, the Crusade's foremost arcanist, guards them."},kw={"armory","cathedral","doan","graveyard","herod","library","mograine","scarlet crusade","scarlet monastery","tirisfal glades","whitemane"},rel={"subzone:scarlet-monastery-cathedral","subzone:scarlet-monastery-armory","subzone:scarlet-monastery-library","subzone:scarlet-monastery-graveyard","npc:sally-whitemane","npc:scarlet-commander-mograine","npc:arcanist-doan","topic:scarlet-crusade"},m={levels="26-45"},src={"Scarlet Monastery","Scarlet Monastery"}}
